<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1334–1369</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Peter the Cruel, Peter I of Castile, Pedro I of Castile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, called the Cruel, was King of Castile and León from 1350 to 1369. His reign was marked by conflict with the nobility and a civil war against his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a>, backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, while Peter was aided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a>, who won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-najera">Battle of Nájera</a> for him in 1367. Henry killed him at Montiel in 1369. Peter built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudejar">Mudéjar</a> palace in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcazar-of-seville">Alcázar of Seville</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile.jpg" alt="Peter of Castile" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre I (1334-1369 ; roi de Castille et de León). Autorité émettrice de monnaie Séville (Espagne ; atelier monétaire... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Espagne,_Castille_et_Leon,_Pierre_I,_dobla,_S%C3%A9ville_-_btv1b11335305r_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
